  "content": "<div id=\"readability-page-1\" class=\"page\"><div><main id=\"genesis-content\"><article aria-label=\"Greg Brockman: Inside the 72 Hours That Almost Killed OpenAI\"><div><p><a href=\"https://fs.blog/knowledge-project-podcast/\">The Knowledge Project Podcast</a></p>\n<div>\n<p>The AI race, the future of AGI, and the inside story of OpenAI. </p> <p>Greg Brockman is the co-founder and President of OpenAI, the company behind ChatGPT and GPT-5. He was the first engineer at Stripe before leaving in 2015 to help start OpenAI.</p> <p>In this rare&nbsp;conversation, Greg goes inside the moments that built, and nearly broke, the most important AI company in the world.</p> <div data-player-id=\"yt_player_787580\"> <h3>Featured clips</h3> <div> <div data-time=\"06:05\"> <div> <p><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"160\" src=\"https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.33.24-AM-300x160.png\" alt=\"Breakthrough Moments at OpenAI\" srcset=\"https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.33.24-AM-300x160.png 300w, https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.33.24-AM-768x409.png 768w, https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.33.24-AM-1024x546.png 1024w, https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.33.24-AM-1536x819.png 1536w, https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.33.24-AM-2048x1092.png 2048w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\"></p> </div> <p>Breakthrough Moments at OpenAI</p> </div> <div data-time=\"15:44\"> <div> <p><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"164\" src=\"https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.36.03-AM-300x164.png\" alt=\"Sam Altman's Firing\" srcset=\"https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.36.03-AM-300x164.png 300w, https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.36.03-AM-768x419.png 768w, https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.36.03-AM-1024x559.png 1024w, https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.36.03-AM-1536x838.png 1536w, https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.36.03-AM-2048x1118.png 2048w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\"></p> </div> <p>Sam Altman's Firing</p> </div> <div data-time=\"32:22\"> <div> <p><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"166\" src=\"https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.35.38-AM-300x166.png\" alt=\"Is AI Going Parabolic?\" srcset=\"https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.35.38-AM-300x166.png 300w, https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.35.38-AM-768x425.png 768w, https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.35.38-AM-1024x567.png 1024w, https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.35.38-AM-1536x850.png 1536w, https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.35.38-AM-2048x1134.png 2048w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\"></p> </div> <p>Is AI Going Parabolic?</p> </div> <div data-time=\"40:38\"> <div> <p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"165\" src=\"https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.33.45-AM-300x165.png\" alt=\"Why ChatGPT No Longer Shows Reasoning\" srcset=\"https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.33.45-AM-300x165.png 300w, https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.33.45-AM-768x423.png 768w, https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.33.45-AM-1024x564.png 1024w, https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.33.45-AM-1536x845.png 1536w, https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.33.45-AM-2048x1127.png 2048w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\"></p> </div> <p>Why ChatGPT No Longer Shows Reasoning</p> </div> <div data-time=\"01:04:44\"> <div> <p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"161\" src=\"https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.35.22-AM-300x161.png\" alt=\"AI and Job Loss\" srcset=\"https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.35.22-AM-300x161.png 300w, https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.35.22-AM-768x411.png 768w, https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.35.22-AM-1024x548.png 1024w, https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.35.22-AM-1536x822.png 1536w, https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-22-at-1.35.22-AM-2048x1096.png 2048w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\"></p> </div> <p>AI and Job Loss</p> </div> </div> </div> <p><strong>Available Now: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/6JoUcQ1qmAc\">YouTube </a>| <strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/episode/4klBY8VmjDBOGupue4aQyL\">Spotify</a></strong></strong> | <strong><a href=\"https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/greg-brockman-inside-the-72-hours-that-almost-killed-openai/id990149481?i=1000763023401\">Apple Podcasts</a> | <a href=\"https://fs.blog/knowledge-project-podcast-transcripts/greg-brockman/\">Transcript </a></strong></p> <p>Greg explains how the original Napa offsite produced the three-step technical plan OpenAI has followed for a decade and the real reason OpenAI had to abandon its pure nonprofit structure. He then walks through the 72 hours after Sam Altman was fired: where he was when he got the board call, why he quit the same day, how the “Phoenix” backup company was designed at Sam’s house the next morning, and the moment Ilya Sutskever’s tweet changed everything.</p> <p>From there, the conversation turns forward: whether we’re in a global AI race, how much of OpenAI’s own code is now written by AI (“it’s hard to know what percent is&nbsp;<em>not</em>“), why OpenAI stopped showing reasoning traces, what a compute-constrained world means for who gets access to AGI, and Greg’s answer to the question everyone is really asking: <em>What happens to your job?</em></p> <p>+ Check out the <a href=\"https://notes.granola.ai/t/2c35c84f-6eb4-497a-8419-294d92141721-009c2hma\">Granola Notes.</a></p>\n</div></div></article><div>\n<div>\n\n<h2 id=\"h-transcript\">Transcript</h2> <p>Get transcripts, early access, ad-free episodes, and so much more. Learn more or sign up now. </p> <p>Already a member? Head over to the <a href=\"https://fs.blog/prime/\">Members Only area</a> to access transcripts and other Member Only content. </p>\n\n</div> <hr> <div>\n<h2 id=\"h-more-episodes\">More Episodes</h2> </div> <div>\n<div>\n\n</div>\n\n<div>\n\n<h2 id=\"h-the-knowledge-project\">The Knowledge Project</h2> <p>A podcast about mastering the best of what other people have already figured out. The Knowledge Project focuses on insights and lessons that never expire. You’ll walk away from every episode with actionable insights that help you get better results and live a more meaningful life.</p> </div>\n</div> <div>\n<h2>Never miss an episode</h2> <div>\n<p>\n\n<h2 id=\"h-a-podcast-about-mastering-the-best-of-what-other-people-have-already-figured-out\">A podcast about mastering the best of what other people have already figured out.</h2>\n\n</p> </div></div>\n\n</div></main></div></div>",
